From 44cc68619e7f110dd84a600baee8b463c501a709 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 20:57:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath10k: shorten the QMI transaction timeout to the
 vendor's 10 s

Every qmi_txn_wait() in this driver waits up to ATH10K_QMI_TIMEOUT, and the
firmware-restart path takes three of them in a row. At 30 s that is 90 s of
uninterruptible sleep -- and ieee80211_restart_work() holds rtnl_lock() and the
wiphy mutex across all of it, so every netlink user in the system queues behind
the biggest lock the network stack has.

Qualcomm's own driver for this silicon waits 10 s: WLFW_TIMEOUT_MS is 10000 in
icnss.c, on the same WLFW QMI service, so 30 s is not a value the firmware
needs. Ten restores a 4x margin against the 120 s hung-task threshold instead
of 1.33x.

Measured on a Pixel 2 XL (msm8998, WCN3990) 2026-08-20. A firmware restart
began at t=1101 s with a storm of "Unbalanced enable for IRQ" out of
ath10k_snoc_hif_start() under ieee80211_restart_work(). Not one further kernel
log line was emitted on any channel for the next 109 s, and the hardware
watchdog then reset the SoC:

  Kernel panic - not syncing: watchdog pretimeout event
  SMP: failed to stop secondary CPUs 2-3

90 s of QMI waits plus the 20 s watchdog pretimeout accounts for that gap
almost exactly.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/qmi.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/qmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/qmi.c
index f1f33af0170a..56d1c902ae12 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/qmi.c
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 #include "snoc.h"
 
 #define ATH10K_QMI_CLIENT_ID		0x4b4e454c
-#define ATH10K_QMI_TIMEOUT		30
+#define ATH10K_QMI_TIMEOUT		10
 #define SMEM_IMAGE_VERSION_TABLE       469
 #define SMEM_IMAGE_TABLE_CNSS_INDEX     13
 #define SMEM_IMAGE_VERSION_ENTRY_SIZE	128
-- 
2.55.0

